<report>
<line><title>Indirectly Standardized Rates and SMR</title></line>
<line></line>
<table>
<tr><th>Reference rate</th><th>Observed person-time</th><th>Expected deaths</th><th></th></tr>
<block name="groups"><tr><td><inu>group</inu></td><td><in>observed</in></td><td><inu>expected</inu></td><td><in>lb</in></td></tr></block>
<tr><td></td><td></td><td>Total = <in>total</in></td><td></td></tr>
</table>
<line></line>
<line>Standardized Mortality Ratio (SMR) = <inu>ratio</inu></line>
<line><b>SMR (*100 as integer) = <in>smr</in></b></line>
<line><ci>Exact <in>pc</in>% confidence interval = <inu>from</inu> to <inu>to</inu> (<in>from100</in> to <inu>to100</inu>)</ci></line>
<line></line>
<line><pval>Probability of observing <in>qty</in> or more deaths by chance <inp>p_hi</inp></pval></line>
<line><pval>Probability of observing <in>qty</in> or fewer deaths by chance <inp>p_lo</inp></pval></line>
</report>
